From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350-samsung-b2q: 384 MiB default CMA pool

Give the board a linux,cma node as stock has, with 384 MiB instead of
stock's 32 MiB. Stock hands cameras ION's system heap; with mainline,
libcamera's software ISP allocates its output buffers from the CMA heap,
and the 32 MiB default fails at 1080p and full resolution (four
full-resolution RGB frames from the IMX563 are about 190 MiB). The pool
is reusable and, as stock's, below 0xdfffffff.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts
index 1f06a0b..a7c6a79 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-samsung-b2q.dts
@@ -161,6 +161,24 @@
 	};
 
 	reserved-memory {
+		/*
+		 * The default CMA pool, stock's linux,cma node with more room. Stock
+		 * keeps 32 MiB here and gives cameras ION's system heap; libcamera's
+		 * software ISP allocates its output from the CMA heap, and four
+		 * full-resolution RGB frames from the IMX563 alone are about 190 MiB.
+		 * Reusable, so the pages serve movable allocations until a device
+		 * needs them. Below 0xdfffffff as stock's, where 0x9dd00000-0xb96fffff
+		 * is free RAM.
+		 */
+		linux,cma {
+			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
+			alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x00000000 0x0 0xdfffffff>;
+			reusable;
+			alignment = <0x0 0x400000>;
+			size = <0x0 0x18000000>;
+			linux,cma-default;
+		};
+
 		cdsp_secure_heap: memory@80c00000 {
 			reg = <0 0x80c00000 0 0x600000>;
 			no-map;
